==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|lovey|lovie|luvvie}}

===Etymology===
From a phonetic spelling of {{m|en|love}} + {{m|en|-y}}; in the second sense, because this (as a term for darling or sweetheart) is perceived as a common utterance of thespians.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|informal}} {{n-g|An affectionate term of address.}}
#: {{ux|en|Don't cry '''luvvy''', everything will be OK.}}
